\ ***************************************************************************
\ STARGLIDER for the BBC Master - a step of the game: the ST's frame loop
\ (&01F10) in its order (docs/research/st-logic.md, "The main loop")
\
\ The disc's engine (engine.6502) calls step_lists and step_logic, drawing
\ the frame between them on the last step due; the spike calls both in
\ turn (spike_step), for tools/logicrun.mjs to check a whole step against
\ the ST's, and has input_step and frame_show do nothing.
\ ***************************************************************************

\ step_lists: world_render's logic up to the lists, the step's frame to be
\ drawn from them.
.step_lists
    BANK_ANDY BANK_WORLD
    JMP world_lists

\ step_logic: the rest of the ST's frame, each routine in its bank with
\ ANDY: the rest of world_render's logic; read_keys, the stick's move
\ taken first, as the ST's mouse's would be there with the keys';
\ player_flight, object_handlers, animate_shapes, collisions,
\ level_message and frame_end's logic; the step's frame shown, if it drew
\ one; then the post-frame tests, which may go on to a level's change
\ or, the game over, to the next game (at once, until the front end is
\ in).
.step_logic
{
    BANK_ANDY BANK_LOGIC
    JSR world_after
    JSR input_step
    JSR read_keys
    BANK_ANDY BANK_WORLD
    JSR player_flight
    JSR object_handlers
    JSR animate_shapes
    BANK_ANDY BANK_LOGIC
    JSR collisions
    JSR level_message
    JSR frame_end_logic
    JSR frame_show
    \ the post-frame tests (&01F30): a level change first; then a game
    \ that ended in an earlier step ends here, as the ST runs one more
    \ frame whole before it ends
    BANK_ANDY BANK_LOGIC
    LDA game_over : ORA game_over+1 : PHA
    JSR post_frame
    PLA : TAX
    LDA level_changed : BNE level
    TXA : BEQ playing
    JSR new_game
.level
    JMP level_start
.playing
    RTS
}
